1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,492
Your meeting is over.

2
00:00:01,492 --> 00:00:04,908
What did you agree to, and who is doing what next?

3
00:00:06,408 --> 00:00:10,350
Motetto turns meeting audio into notes on your own Mac.

4
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:13,898
No account, no cloud processing, and no meeting bot.

5
00:00:15,398 --> 00:00:21,055
Import a recording, and let local models transcribe the conversation and write the
notes.

6
00:00:21,055 --> 00:00:24,287
This example uses a fictional product launch meeting.

7
00:00:25,787 --> 00:00:27,924
Review the decisions and action items.

8
00:00:27,924 --> 00:00:32,911
Click a source timestamp to jump to the transcript and hear the original words.

9
00:00:33,537 --> 00:00:38,637
Original meeting audio: Alex will finish the welcome screen
and the first run checklist by Friday.

10
00:00:40,287 --> 00:00:44,009
Check off a finished task, or edit the notes in place.

11
00:00:44,009 --> 00:00:46,378
Your meeting stays useful after the call.

12
00:00:47,878 --> 00:00:49,920
Need to share a specific moment?

13
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:53,664
Select a passage in the transcript and save an audio clip.

14
00:00:55,164 --> 00:00:59,515
Your audio, transcript, and notes stay as files on your computer.

15
00:00:59,515 --> 00:01:01,888
Keep control of your meeting history.

16
00:01:03,388 --> 00:01:05,049
Motetto is in early development.

17
00:01:05,049 --> 00:01:11,691
Explore the source on GitHub, try it on your Mac, and tell us what would make your next
meeting easier.
